# What the package builders and their checks run in and against, by digest or
# commit. Read by build-rpm.sh, build-pacman.sh and tests/packaging/*. A tag or
# a branch is a moving name, so a check could land in another environment with
# nothing in history saying which, and each image and commit here is fixed. What
# is installed on top of an image is not, except the fakeroot of the pacman
# builder, which comes from the Arch Linux Archive of the day of its image:
# rpm-build and the tools of the checks come from the repositories of the
# distribution as they are that day.
#
# Every image here is also a line of .github/ci-images/Dockerfile, which is what
# Dependabot watches, and `ci_images/images.py sync` copies a new digest over.
#
#   AlmaLinux 9     rpm 4.16: writes package format 4 and is the oldest rpm the
#                   channel serves (EL 9). The index digest, so the same line
#                   works on an x86_64 and an arm64 runner.
#   Fedora 45       rpm 6: reads the RPMFORMAT tag the channel's admission
#                   needs (rpm 4.16 does not know that tag).
#   Arch Linux      makepkg, bsdtar and zstd. The builder reads the day of the
#                   image from its version label and takes fakeroot from the
#                   Arch Linux Archive of that day.
#   Channel commits the admission each channel runs, checked out at this commit
#                   and run over the packages built here. Move them when the
#                   channel's admission changes.
RPM_BUILD_BASE="docker.io/library/almalinux:9@sha256:02df05719ef287ebd0df0a1eedb9172a00bd70703aed7b25660e426b8e0d6047"
RPM_QUERY_IMAGE="docker.io/library/fedora:45@sha256:a7d72ba2745b100a3351087472e5ee7b2450af7cf331e7673007e3817612839c"
PACMAN_BUILD_BASE="docker.io/library/archlinux:base@sha256:375a401bb3c6376b37f40b6dfa25067db37ec78d0b7af67ae6315f43a0184a9d"
RPM_CHANNEL_COMMIT="df26a81e5f67bce74d056fceaf11f2e1c7553816"
PACMAN_CHANNEL_COMMIT="212e32bb91026d35ee9429c25e9f0c80c517e9a0"
